1. Pink Trombone (the source of the tube, the glottis and the anatomy)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
monk_mouth's tube, its glottis and its anatomy are adapted from Pink
Trombone, "bare-handed procedural speech synthesis", version 1.1, March 2017,
by Neil Thapen, rewritten in float32 C++ and changed as noted below:

    https://dood.al/pinktrombone/

What comes from it:

  - the tube (src/core/mm_tube.*): the Kelly-Lochbaum waveguide of
    Tract.runStep — junction scattering, the glottal and lip reflections,
    the fixed-profile nose branch and its three-port junction, and the
    reflection-coefficient interpolation — run here at 22 sections x 1 step
    per sample instead of the reference's 44 x 2.
  - the glottis (src/core/mm_glottis.*): the Liljencrants-Fant pulse set-up
    of Glottis.setupWaveform, line for line, and the noise modulator of
    Glottis.getNoiseModulator (src/core/mm_noise.h).
  - the anatomy (src/core/mm_body.*): the tongue curve of
    TractUI.setRestDiameter, the constriction shape of TractUI.handleTouches,
    the throat / lip / velum landmarks, the release transient of
    Tract.addTransient and the turbulence window of
    Tract.addTurbulenceNoiseAtIndex, all re-expressed as fractions of tract
    length.
  - the vowel pose seeds in src/core/mm_vocab.cpp were read from the labels
    of TractUI.drawPositions.

Everything else — the body's dynamics, the pitch axis, the vocabulary's
tuning, the score compiler and player, the whistle, the Teensy wrapper — is
not from Pink Trombone, and nothing is ported from anywhere else.

